course: dictionary
lesson: 8484
title: Sandal and its context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A sandal is an open shoe, held on the foot with straps, and it is worn in warm weather. When you meet a word you do not know, read the words around it. If a text says the family packed swimming costumes and sandals for the beach, the clues show that sandals are summer shoes.
explain: Some things have different names in different places. «Des tongs are flip-flops, which Australians call thongs and New Zealanders call jandals; des sandales are sandals.» So flip-flops and sandals are different shoes, even though both are worn in summer. Context and a dictionary together can sort this out.
explain: Context can also warn you about safety. Sandals do not protect your toes, so a careful writer who says the children wore sandals on a rocky hill is telling you something. Ask yourself: would this shoe keep my feet safe here?
fact: A sandal is an open shoe held on the foot with straps, worn in warm weather.
fact: The plural is sandals, as in «a pair of sandals».
fact: Sandal can also mean sandalwood, a sweet-smelling wood, but this meaning is less common.
fact: In ancient lands like Egypt and Rome, people wore sandals.
fact: Sandals do not protect your toes, so they are not good for hiking on rocks or in workshops.
exercise: What is a sandal? | A thick winter boot with laces up to the knee | A warm glove for snow | *An open shoe held on the foot with straps, worn in warm weather | A hat worn for sunshine
exercise: Why are sandals a poor choice for hiking on rocks? | Sandals are only worn in winter | Sandals are too heavy to carry | *Sandals do not protect your toes
exercise: Mia from Sydney says, «I left my thongs at the beach.» What are thongs here? | *Flip-flops | Long socks | Boots for snow | A kitchen tool for picking up food
test: Which word names an open shoe worn in warm weather? | Boot | Glove | Sock | *Sandal
test: In ancient lands like Egypt and Rome, what did people wear on their feet? | *Sandals | Trainers with spikes | Snow boots | Ski boots
exam: Why should you not wear sandals in a workshop? | *Sandals do not protect your toes | Sandals make a loud noise | Sandals are too heavy | Sandals are too warm
